WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.650
In September 2024, the UK closed
its last coal power station.

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:12.450
Per person, EDGAR estimates UK
emissions fell from 13.27 tonnes of CO₂

3
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:18.010
equivalent in 1990 to 5.45 in 2025.

4
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:24.210
In total, the UK's emissions fell by
54 per cent between 1990 and 2025,

5
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.530
on provisional figures.

6
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.550
So has the UK really halved
its part in climate change?

7
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.150
Or do fewer people simply live there?

8
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.600
In this mission, you'll see how far
greenhouse gases have climbed above their

9
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.210
pre-industrial levels.

10
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.950
Then you'll rank the
world's emitters in total,

11
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.450
per person and through history,
and watch the order change.

12
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.800
Your mission: decide whether the UK has
really halved its part in climate change.
